1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,800
Football broadcasts tell you what happened. Nobody tells you why it mattered.

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:18,800
Underneath is a world we can run forwards, backwards and sideways.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:26,000
Each key moment is replayed 200 times. Passing instead of shooting: +4 points of win chance.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,400
Not a stat: what would have happened.

5
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:38,300
Every refereeing call explained, with the lines drawn.

6
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:46,300
Agents share a blackboard, reach data only through MCP, and every number is checked in code before it airs.

7
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:54,300
Kill the newsroom mid-moment and it resumes from its checkpoint.

8
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:03,300
It sees danger before it happens...

9
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:09,300
...and tells the studio what the manager should do.

10
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:21,300
The same intelligence becomes an analyst's breakdown, a casual fan's line, and a player's story.

11
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:33,300
A producer can veto anything before it airs.

12
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:46,300
Measured, not claimed: 141 of 141 on-screen numbers grounded, 500 of 500 planted errors caught, $2.31 for the golden match.

